    "narrative": "The offensive engine for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (69.89) and **Austin Riley** (69.46). **Corbin Carroll** remains an essential start despite the platoon disadvantage against Gamboa; his elite sprint speed profile provides a floor that renders his 69.89 score highly bankable, bolstered by a significant boost from hitting out of the #2 spot. **Austin Riley** presents the day\u2019s most fascinating upside case; while his #8 lineup position creates a slight drag, he is facing a targetable 4.81 xERA in Ober and benefits from a favorable wind-out environment, pushing his efficiency score well into the \"Strong\" territory. **Seiya Suzuki** also warrants attention at 61.27, as he effectively manages a tough matchup against Castillo by leveraging a park-factor bump that keeps him as a recommended start.\n\nThe lineup construction is defensive against a volatile slate, leaving **Zach McKinstry** (48.85) and **Max Muncy** (53.17) in the marginal bucket. While **Max Muncy** has the power ceiling to exceed his projection, his #7 spot against Wacha suppresses his overall efficiency. Decisions regarding the bench remain heavily influenced by our injury report, with **James Wood**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Vinnie Pasquantino** all sidelined. Because of these constraints, we are operating with a shortened roster, and no active bench players pushed hard enough to displace our current starters. We are closely monitoring the status of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Henry Bolte**; both currently carry \"Lineup Pending\" tags, and should their actual batting orders drop significantly lower than our projected #3 and #1 spots respectively, their efficiency scores will need to be re-evaluated to prevent unnecessary depletion of our weekly game caps.",
